Started NetHack about a year ago. Quit after maybe two weeks of
on-and-off frustration. Started up again about 6 weeks ago. Read that
Barbs were the easiest so started with them. Died a lot. Switched to
Samurais because I liked having a shield (or so I thought). Died a lot
more but learned the game. Switched back to Barbs and now ascended
after a few tries.

This game went almost completely painlessly except for the Astral
Plane. I decided to do Soko first and, lo and behold, I find a
luckstone sitting there on DL3 about 10 steps away from a general
store. I get the amulet from Soko, head to Minetown. Skip Mine's End
cuz I got a luckstone already. I find an aligned altar on DL10 ready
equipped with a priest, a chest, and a bones pile from a previous
barbarian. I didn't get any necessities from the bones pile but I got
some fodder for alchemy and scrolls.

I sacrifice until I get Cleaver and then on the next sac I get crowned!
I head down to the Castle with no problems at all, get the /oW and make
my first wishes. Later on, I find a magic lamp and get another wish.
All in total, I get 7 wishes: ?oCharging, GDSM, speed boots,
?oGenocide, Helm of Opposite Alignment (I was worried about Astral),
Master Key of Thievery, and something else which I can't remember.

I head back up, enchant up my crap, beat down the Quest with ease. Back
down, I move through Genn very easily. Hit all the standard stops with
no problems. In the Sanctum, the High Priest wasn't there and I
realized Yeenoghu took the Amulet. Had to chase him up a few stairs to
take it back.

I make it all the way up getting warped back only about 4 times. The
Elemental Planes go by with virtually no issues. I got engulfed about a
million times on Air but it just annoyed me more than anything else.

I get to Astral, put on blind, and I see Death and Famine nearby. I
quickly move away from Death toward Famine. Famine attacks and I
realize (a) I forgot to take food out of my bag (b) I forgot to take
healing potions out.

Hit! I'm down to 100hp and starving. I pull food out. 60hp. I eat.
40hp. I pull out a full healing potion. 13hp.... I quaff it and then
proceed to slap down Famine (twice apparently although I dont remember
that. Must have been a stray death ray).

I head to the right, open the door, and THANK YOU it's aligned. I zap a
death ray to clear a path, run in and boom. I'm done!

Besides getting lucky against Famine, the run went completely
painlessly. Cheers to using the n00b class!


